nodes.statement:
The crucial property of the equation $p(x,y,n)=x^{2}-y^{2}-n^{2}$ is that its solutions can be parameterized as
  \begin{equation} \nonumber
  \begin{split}
          x=\gamma\alpha(\alpha+2\beta), y=\gamma(\alpha+(1+i)\beta)(\alpha+(1-i)\beta),\alpha,\beta,\gamma\in\mathbb{Z}[i].
   \end{split}
   \end{equation}

assumptions:
$p$ be a quadratic equation of the form
    \begin{equation}\nonumber
    \begin{split}
      p(x,y,n)=ax^{2}+by^{2}+cn^{2}+dxy+exn+fyn
    \end{split}
  \end{equation}
  for some $a,b,c,d,e,f\in\mathbb{Z}[i]$

