onumber  egin{split} \alpha'_{i}\coloneqq \omega_{i}^{-1}\alpha_{i}^{p}\gamma_{i}^{-1}\in H^{\underline{ old{k}}}, 	ext{ for all } 1\leq i\leq d-1. \end{split} \end{equation} By assumption, there exists an $S$-frequency nilcharacter $f$ with $\Vert f\Vert_{Lip(H)}\leq 1$ such that  egin{equation}  egin{split} \Bigl\vert\mathbb{E}_{n\in[N]} old{1}_{P}(n)f(g_{1}(n)\cdot e_{Y})\Bigr\vert>\kappa \end{split} \end{equation} for some arithmetic progression $P\subset[N]$. We define  egin{equation}
