Since $g_{1}(n)=\prod_{i=0}^{d}\alpha_{i}^{\binom{n}{i}}$, it is easy to verify that there exist elements $h_{0}\in H, v_{1},\dots,v_{d}\in H_{2}\subset H^{\underline{\bold{k}}}$, a universal constant $K>0$ depending only on $d$, and polynomials $p_{1},\dots,p_{d-1}$, $q_{1},\dots,q_{d-1}$
